<quiz>
  <question type="multichoice">
    <name>
      <text>NEET_UG_BIOLOGY_SEXUAL_REPRODUCTION_IN_FLOWERING_PLANTS_MCQ_Q01 - Identification of microsporangial wall layers</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[
<p>The diagram given below represents a transverse section of a portion of a young microsporangium showing four concentric wall layers labeled <strong>A</strong>, <strong>B</strong>, <strong>C</strong>, and <strong>D</strong>:</p>
<div style="text-align:center; margin:15px 0;">
  <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 540 320" width="100%" max-width="540px" height="auto" style="background:#fdfdfd; border:1px solid #dcdcdc; border-radius:6px; font-family:Arial, sans-serif;">
    <defs>
      <radialGradient id="sporGrad" cx="50%" cy="50%" r="50%">
        <stop offset="0%" stop-color="#fff3b0"/>
        <stop offset="100%" stop-color="#f6d365"/>
      </radialGradient>
    </defs>
    <!-- Sporogenous tissue core -->
    <path d="M 220 80 Q 320 80 340 180 Q 320 270 220 270 Q 150 250 150 175 Q 150 100 220 80 Z" fill="url(#sporGrad)" stroke="#d4ac0d" stroke-width="2"/>
    <text x="235" y="170" font-size="13" font-weight="bold" fill="#7d6608" text-anchor="middle">Sporogenous</text>
    <text x="235" y="188" font-size="13" font-weight="bold" fill="#7d6608" text-anchor="middle">Tissue</text>
    
    <!-- Layer D: Tapetum -->
    <path d="M 190 55 Q 355 55 375 180 Q 355 295 190 295 Q 115 270 115 175 Q 115 80 190 55 Z" fill="none" stroke="#27ae60" stroke-width="14" stroke-dasharray="4,2"/>
    
    <!-- Layer C: Middle layers -->
    <path d="M 175 40 Q 380 40 400 180 Q 380 310 175 310 Q 95 285 95 175 Q 95 65 175 40 Z" fill="none" stroke="#85929e" stroke-width="12"/>
    
    <!-- Layer B: Endothecium -->
    <path d="M 160 25 Q 405 25 425 180 Q 405 325 160 325 Q 75 300 75 175 Q 75 50 160 25 Z" fill="none" stroke="#2980b9" stroke-width="14"/>
    
    <!-- Layer A: Epidermis -->
    <path d="M 145 10 Q 430 10 450 180 Q 430 340 145 340 Q 55 315 55 175 Q 55 35 145 10 Z" fill="none" stroke="#c0392b" stroke-width="10"/>

    <!-- Pointer lines & labels -->
    <!-- Label A: Epidermis -->
    <line x1="445" y1="90" x2="490" y2="60" stroke="#c0392b" stroke-width="1.8"/>
    <circle cx="445" cy="90" r="3.5" fill="#c0392b"/>
    <text x="495" y="65" font-size="15" font-weight="bold" fill="#c0392b">A</text>

    <!-- Label B: Endothecium -->
    <line x1="418" y1="120" x2="490" y2="110" stroke="#2980b9" stroke-width="1.8"/>
    <circle cx="418" cy="120" r="3.5" fill="#2980b9"/>
    <text x="495" y="115" font-size="15" font-weight="bold" fill="#2980b9">B</text>

    <!-- Label C: Middle layers -->
    <line x1="392" y1="150" x2="490" y2="160" stroke="#85929e" stroke-width="1.8"/>
    <circle cx="392" cy="150" r="3.5" fill="#85929e"/>
    <text x="495" y="165" font-size="15" font-weight="bold" fill="#566573">C</text>

    <!-- Label D: Tapetum -->
    <line x1="365" y1="180" x2="490" y2="210" stroke="#27ae60" stroke-width="1.8"/>
    <circle cx="365" cy="180" r="3.5" fill="#27ae60"/>
    <text x="495" y="215" font-size="15" font-weight="bold" fill="#27ae60">D</text>
  </svg>
</div>
<p>Which of the following correctly identifies wall layers <strong>A</strong>, <strong>B</strong>, <strong>C</strong>, and <strong>D</strong> from the periphery towards the centre?</p>
]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[
<p><strong>Step 1: Understand the anatomical organisation of microsporangial wall layers.</strong><br/>In a transverse section, a typical angiosperm microsporangium is bounded by four distinct wall layers arranged concentrically from the periphery to the centre:
1. Epidermis (outermost single protective tier)
2. Endothecium (sub-epidermal layer assisting in anther dehiscence)
3. Middle layers (one to three short-lived cellular tiers)
4. Tapetum (innermost nutritive wall layer enclosing the sporogenous cells)</p>
<p><strong>Step 2: Match the labeled positions in the diagrammatic section.</strong><br/>Tracing the concentric layers from outer surface to inner core:
- Structure A is the outermost bounding layer, representing the <strong>Epidermis</strong>.
- Structure B is the layer immediately beneath the epidermis, representing the <strong>Endothecium</strong>.
- Structure C represents the intermediate 1–3 tiers, which are the <strong>Middle layers</strong>.
- Structure D is the innermost layer directly lining the sporogenous tissue, representing the <strong>Tapetum</strong>.</p>
<p><strong>Step 3: State the final conclusion.</strong><br/>The correct identification in centrifugal to centripetal order is: A = Epidermis, B = Endothecium, C = Middle layers, and D = Tapetum.</p>
]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>4.0000000</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.2500000</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <single>true</single>
    <shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers>
    <answernumbering>abc</answernumbering>
    <answer fraction="100" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>A = Epidermis, B = Endothecium, C = Middle layers, D = Tapetum</p>]]></text>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>A = Endothecium, B = Epidermis, C = Middle layers, D = Tapetum</p>]]></text>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>A = Epidermis, B = Middle layers, C = Endothecium, D = Tapetum</p>]]></text>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>A = Tapetum, B = Middle layers, C = Endothecium, D = Epidermis</p>]]></text>
    </answer>
