  <question type="multichoice">
    <name>
      <text>NEET_UG_BIOLOGY_SEXUAL_REPRODUCTION_IN_FLOWERING_PLANTS_MCQ_Q02 - Anatomical regions of an anatropous ovule</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[
<p>Examine the diagrammatic view of a typical anatropous ovule given below:</p>
<div style="text-align:center; margin:15px 0;">
  <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 460 380" width="100%" max-width="460px" height="auto" style="background:#ffffff; border:1px solid #dcdcdc; border-radius:6px; font-family:Arial, sans-serif;">
    <!-- Stalk (Funicle) -->
    <path d="M 140 330 C 135 250 145 160 170 120 L 195 125 C 170 170 160 250 165 330 Z" fill="#b7e4c7" stroke="#2d6a4f" stroke-width="1.8"/>
    <!-- Outer Body of Ovule -->
    <path d="M 190 115 C 205 30 350 30 360 180 C 370 310 240 335 200 300 C 190 290 195 270 205 260 C 235 275 320 270 325 180 C 330 90 230 80 190 115 Z" fill="#d8f3dc" stroke="#2d6a4f" stroke-width="2"/>
    <!-- Inner Integument -->
    <path d="M 215 140 C 240 95 305 95 310 180 C 315 250 250 255 220 235 L 222 215 C 245 225 290 220 288 180 C 285 125 240 120 215 140 Z" fill="#e9edc9" stroke="#588157" stroke-width="1.5"/>
    <!-- Nucellus -->
    <ellipse cx="258" cy="180" rx="36" ry="48" fill="#fefae0" stroke="#b7b7a4" stroke-width="1.5"/>
    <!-- Embryo Sac -->
    <ellipse cx="258" cy="180" rx="20" ry="32" fill="#fff" stroke="#bc6c25" stroke-width="1.8"/>
    <circle cx="258" cy="165" r="3" fill="#bc6c25"/>
    <circle cx="258" cy="195" r="3" fill="#bc6c25"/>

    <!-- Label A: Hilum -->
    <line x1="168" y1="130" x2="80" y2="100" stroke="#1d3557" stroke-width="1.8"/>
    <circle cx="168" cy="130" r="3.5" fill="#1d3557"/>
    <text x="60" y="105" font-size="16" font-weight="bold" fill="#1d3557">A</text>

    <!-- Label B: Micropyle -->
    <line x1="205" y1="285" x2="110" y2="285" stroke="#1d3557" stroke-width="1.8"/>
    <circle cx="205" cy="285" r="3.5" fill="#1d3557"/>
    <text x="90" y="290" font-size="16" font-weight="bold" fill="#1d3557">B</text>

    <!-- Label C: Chalaza -->
    <line x1="285" y1="45" x2="380" y2="45" stroke="#1d3557" stroke-width="1.8"/>
    <circle cx="285" cy="45" r="3.5" fill="#1d3557"/>
    <text x="395" y="50" font-size="16" font-weight="bold" fill="#1d3557">C</text>

    <!-- Label D: Nucellus -->
    <line x1="285" y1="150" x2="380" y2="150" stroke="#1d3557" stroke-width="1.8"/>
    <circle cx="285" cy="150" r="3.5" fill="#1d3557"/>
    <text x="395" y="155" font-size="16" font-weight="bold" fill="#1d3557">D</text>
  </svg>
</div>
<p>Which one of the following options correctly matches the labels <strong>A</strong>, <strong>B</strong>, <strong>C</strong>, and <strong>D</strong> with their descriptions?</p>
]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[
<p><strong>Step 1: Identify the anatomical parts of the anatropous ovule from the diagram.</strong><br/>- <strong>Label A</strong> points to the junction where the stalk (funicle) fuses with the body of the ovule, which defines the <strong>Hilum</strong>.<br/>- <strong>Label B</strong> points to the narrow opening at the tip left uncovered by the integuments, known as the <strong>Micropyle</strong>.<br/>- <strong>Label C</strong> points to the basal region of the ovule directly opposite the micropylar end, which represents the <strong>Chalaza</strong>.<br/>- <strong>Label D</strong> points to the central nutritive cellular mass enclosed within the protective integuments, which is the <strong>Nucellus</strong>.</p>
<p><strong>Step 2: Verify the roles and relationships of each region.</strong><br/>The hilum bridges the funicle and the main body of the ovule. The micropylar canal serves as the entry pathway for the pollen tube into the ovule. The chalaza establishes the botanical base of the ovule. The nucellus contains abundant reserve food materials and houses the developing female gametophyte.</p>
<p><strong>Step 3: State the final conclusion.</strong><br/>The correct match is: A = Hilum, B = Micropyle, C = Chalaza, and D = Nucellus.</p>
]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
