  <question type="multichoice">
    <name>
      <text>NEET_UG_BIOLOGY_SEXUAL_REPRODUCTION_IN_FLOWERING_PLANTS_MCQ_Q03 - Cellular components of mature angiosperm female gametophyte</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[
<p>The diagram below illustrates the mature 7-celled, 8-nucleate female gametophyte (embryo sac) of an angiosperm:</p>
<div style="text-align:center; margin:15px 0;">
  <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 380 440" width="100%" max-width="380px" height="auto" style="background:#ffffff; border:1px solid #dcdcdc; border-radius:6px; font-family:Arial, sans-serif;">
    <!-- Embryo sac boundary -->
    <rect x="70" y="20" width="240" height="400" rx="120" ry="120" fill="#f8f9fa" stroke="#2c3e50" stroke-width="2.5"/>
    
    <!-- Chalazal Antipodals (P) -->
    <path d="M 120 40 Q 150 75 190 70 Q 230 75 260 40 Z" fill="#d5f5e3" stroke="#27ae60" stroke-width="1.8"/>
    <circle cx="150" cy="52" r="5" fill="#e74c3c"/>
    <circle cx="190" cy="58" r="5" fill="#e74c3c"/>
    <circle cx="230" cy="52" r="5" fill="#e74c3c"/>
    <text x="190" y="30" font-size="12" fill="#7f8c8d" text-anchor="middle">Chalazal End</text>

    <!-- Polar Nuclei in Central Cell (Q) -->
    <ellipse cx="178" cy="180" rx="14" ry="16" fill="#fadbd8" stroke="#e74c3c" stroke-width="1.5"/>
    <circle cx="178" cy="180" r="4.5" fill="#78281f"/>
    <ellipse cx="202" cy="180" rx="14" ry="16" fill="#fadbd8" stroke="#e74c3c" stroke-width="1.5"/>
    <circle cx="202" cy="180" r="4.5" fill="#78281f"/>

    <!-- Egg Cell (R) -->
    <circle cx="190" cy="310" r="22" fill="#fdebd0" stroke="#d35400" stroke-width="1.8"/>
    <circle cx="190" cy="305" r="5" fill="#6e2c00"/>

    <!-- Synergids flanking egg cell -->
    <path d="M 125 365 C 120 310 160 305 168 340 C 170 370 145 375 125 365 Z" fill="#ebf5fb" stroke="#2980b9" stroke-width="1.5"/>
    <circle cx="145" cy="335" r="4" fill="#1b4f72"/>
    <path d="M 255 365 C 260 310 220 305 212 340 C 210 370 235 375 255 365 Z" fill="#ebf5fb" stroke="#2980b9" stroke-width="1.5"/>
    <circle cx="235" cy="335" r="4" fill="#1b4f72"/>

    <!-- Filiform Apparatus (S) -->
    <path d="M 130 365 Q 145 385 145 400 M 140 365 Q 155 385 155 402 M 250 365 Q 235 385 235 400 M 240 365 Q 225 385 225 402" fill="none" stroke="#2980b9" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round"/>
    <text x="190" y="415" font-size="12" fill="#7f8c8d" text-anchor="middle">Micropylar End</text>

    <!-- Pointer P: Antipodals -->
    <line x1="245" y1="55" x2="320" y2="55" stroke="#1d3557" stroke-width="1.8"/>
    <circle cx="245" cy="55" r="3.5" fill="#1d3557"/>
    <text x="330" y="60" font-size="16" font-weight="bold" fill="#1d3557">P</text>

    <!-- Pointer Q: Polar nuclei -->
    <line x1="216" y1="180" x2="320" y2="180" stroke="#1d3557" stroke-width="1.8"/>
    <circle cx="216" cy="180" r="3.5" fill="#1d3557"/>
    <text x="330" y="185" font-size="16" font-weight="bold" fill="#1d3557">Q</text>

    <!-- Pointer R: Egg cell -->
    <line x1="168" y1="310" x2="30" y2="310" stroke="#1d3557" stroke-width="1.8"/>
    <circle cx="168" cy="310" r="3.5" fill="#1d3557"/>
    <text x="12" y="315" font-size="16" font-weight="bold" fill="#1d3557">R</text>

    <!-- Pointer S: Filiform apparatus -->
    <line x1="145" y1="390" x2="30" y2="390" stroke="#1d3557" stroke-width="1.8"/>
    <circle cx="145" cy="390" r="3.5" fill="#1d3557"/>
    <text x="12" y="395" font-size="16" font-weight="bold" fill="#1d3557">S</text>
  </svg>
</div>
<p>Select the option that correctly identifies the labeled structures along with their correct functional attribute:</p>
]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[
<p><strong>Step 1: Identify labeled structure P.</strong><br/>Structure P represents the group of three cells situated at the chalazal end, known as the <strong>Antipodals</strong>.</p>
<p><strong>Step 2: Identify labeled structure Q.</strong><br/>Structure Q represents the two <strong>Polar nuclei</strong> situated within the large central cell below the egg apparatus, which subsequently participate in triple fusion to produce the primary endosperm nucleus (PEN).</p>
<p><strong>Step 3: Identify labeled structure R.</strong><br/>Structure R represents the haploid <strong>Egg cell</strong> located centrally in the egg apparatus at the micropylar end, which fuses with a male gamete during syngamy to generate the diploid zygote.</p>
<p><strong>Step 4: Identify labeled structure S.</strong><br/>Structure S represents the <strong>Filiform apparatus</strong>, specialized finger-like cellular thickenings present at the micropylar tip of the synergids, which plays a pivotal role in guiding the entry of the pollen tube into the synergid.</p>
<p><strong>Step 5: Conclude the final match.</strong><br/>The identity of the labels is: P = Antipodals, Q = Polar nuclei, R = Egg cell, and S = Filiform apparatus (responsible for guiding pollen tube entry).</p>
]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
