  <question type="multichoice">
    <name>
      <text>NEET_UG_BIOLOGY_SEXUAL_REPRODUCTION_IN_FLOWERING_PLANTS_MCQ_Q04 - Structural parts of monocotyledonous grass embryo</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[
<p>The diagram given below depicts a longitudinal section through an embryo of grass (monocotyledon):</p>
<div style="text-align:center; margin:15px 0;">
  <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 360 460" width="100%" max-width="360px" height="auto" style="background:#ffffff; border:1px solid #dcdcdc; border-radius:6px; font-family:Arial, sans-serif;">
    <!-- Scutellum (A) -->
    <path d="M 170 30 C 130 50 110 110 100 200 C 90 290 120 370 160 410 C 145 370 135 280 145 190 C 150 120 165 70 170 30 Z" fill="#d4efdf" stroke="#27ae60" stroke-width="2"/>
    
    <!-- Coleoptile (B) -->
    <path d="M 180 80 C 180 60 230 60 235 130 L 205 140 C 200 100 180 95 180 80 Z" fill="#fcf3cf" stroke="#f39c12" stroke-width="1.8"/>
    
    <!-- Shoot Apex & leaf primordia -->
    <path d="M 195 110 Q 210 105 215 135 L 195 140 Z" fill="#a9dfbf" stroke="#196f3d" stroke-width="1.2"/>
    
    <!-- Epiblast -->
    <path d="M 230 230 C 245 220 245 250 235 260 Z" fill="#ebedef" stroke="#7f8c8d" stroke-width="1.5"/>
    
    <!-- Radicle & Root Cap (C) -->
    <path d="M 185 280 L 210 280 L 210 330 C 210 345 185 345 185 330 Z" fill="#fadbd8" stroke="#c0392b" stroke-width="1.8"/>
    <path d="M 180 325 C 180 355 215 355 215 325 Z" fill="#f5b7b1" stroke="#922b21" stroke-width="1.2"/>

    <!-- Coleorrhiza (D) -->
    <path d="M 165 265 C 165 390 235 390 235 270" fill="none" stroke="#8e44ad" stroke-width="2" stroke-dasharray="4,2"/>

    <!-- Pointer A: Scutellum -->
    <line x1="120" y1="120" x2="45" y2="90" stroke="#1d3557" stroke-width="1.8"/>
    <circle cx="120" cy="120" r="3.5" fill="#1d3557"/>
    <text x="25" y="95" font-size="16" font-weight="bold" fill="#1d3557">A</text>

    <!-- Pointer B: Coleoptile -->
    <line x1="225" y1="85" x2="295" y2="85" stroke="#1d3557" stroke-width="1.8"/>
    <circle cx="225" cy="85" r="3.5" fill="#1d3557"/>
    <text x="310" y="90" font-size="16" font-weight="bold" fill="#1d3557">B</text>

    <!-- Pointer C: Radicle / Root cap -->
    <line x1="210" y1="315" x2="295" y2="315" stroke="#1d3557" stroke-width="1.8"/>
    <circle cx="210" cy="315" r="3.5" fill="#1d3557"/>
    <text x="310" y="320" font-size="16" font-weight="bold" fill="#1d3557">C</text>

    <!-- Pointer D: Coleorrhiza -->
    <line x1="200" y1="375" x2="295" y2="375" stroke="#1d3557" stroke-width="1.8"/>
    <circle cx="200" cy="375" r="3.5" fill="#1d3557"/>
    <text x="310" y="380" font-size="16" font-weight="bold" fill="#1d3557">D</text>
  </svg>
</div>
<p>Which of the following statements regarding the labeled structures is <strong>correct</strong>?</p>
]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[
<p><strong>Step 1: Identify the labeled structures of the grass embryo.</strong><br/>- Structure A is the large, shield-shaped single lateral cotyledon, termed the <strong>Scutellum</strong>.<br/>- Structure B is the hollow foliar sheath enclosing the shoot apex and leaf primordia above the level of scutellum attachment, known as the <strong>Coleoptile</strong>.<br/>- Structure C points to the embryonic root tip, comprising the <strong>Radicle and root cap</strong>.<br/>- Structure D represents the undifferentiated basal sheath enclosing the radicle and root cap, known as the <strong>Coleorrhiza</strong>.</p>
<p><strong>Step 2: Evaluate the functional and structural attributes.</strong><br/>- The single cotyledon of the grass family is called the scutellum and occupies a lateral position along the embryonal axis.<br/>- The coleoptile encloses the epicotyl and shoot apex in a hollow foliar structure.<br/>- The coleorrhiza is an undifferentiated protective sheath enclosing the radicle and root cap at the lower end of the embryonal axis.<br/>- A statement asserting that A represents the scutellum (cotyledon), B is the coleoptile protecting the shoot apex, C represents the radicle/root cap, and D is the coleorrhiza accurately reflects the morphology described in the text.</p>
<p><strong>Step 3: State the final conclusion.</strong><br/>Structure A is the scutellum (single lateral cotyledon), B is the coleoptile (foliar sheath covering shoot apex), C is the radicle/root cap, and D is the coleorrhiza (protective sheath covering radicle and root cap).</p>
]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>4.0000000</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.2500000</penalty>
